WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.541
Threat hunting is a proactive process of searching for evidence of malicious

00:00:04.541 --> 00:00:07.501
activity that may already exist within an environment.

00:00:07.501 --> 00:00:12.682
It is disciplined investigation, not guesswork or a dramatic search for clues without evidence.

00:00:12.682 --> 00:00:16.383
Unlike routine alert response, hunts often begin with a hypothesis.

00:00:16.383 --> 00:00:20.824
A hunter may ask whether a suspicious behavior could be occurring quietly,

00:00:20.824 --> 00:00:23.044
whether an account is being misused,

00:00:23.044 --> 00:00:26.745
or whether a technique could leave traces in available telemetry.

00:00:26.745 --> 00:00:30.076
The proactive nature of hunting changes the starting point.

00:00:30.076 --> 00:00:35.257
Instead of waiting for an alert to define the investigation, hunters use threat intelligence,

00:00:35.257 --> 00:00:39.328
environmental knowledge, adversary behavior, and prior incidents to form useful questions.

00:00:39.328 --> 00:00:43.398
Threat hunting focuses on uncovering hidden threats through systematic investigation, analysis,

00:00:43.398 --> 00:00:44.509
and evidence gathering.

00:00:44.509 --> 00:00:48.949
The result may be an incident, a detection improvement, a documented gap,

00:00:48.949 --> 00:00:51.540
or stronger confidence in an existing control.
